\description{
Loads season-level WNBA team rosters scraped from the WNBA
Stats API. One row per athlete-team-season triple. Backed by the
\code{wehoop-wnba-stats-data} pipeline that reads raw JSONs from
\code{wehoop-wnba-stats-raw} and publishes parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{wnba_stats_rosters} release tag.

Loads season-level WNBA coaching staff data scraped from the
WNBA Stats API. One row per coach-team-season triple. Backed by the
\code{wehoop-wnba-stats-data} pipeline that reads raw JSONs from
\code{wehoop-wnba-stats-raw} and publishes parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{wnba_stats_coaches} release tag.

\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#deprecated}{\figure{lifecycle-deprecated.svg}{options: alt='[Deprecated]'}}}{\strong{[Deprecated]}} Loads season-level WNBA
player statistics. \strong{Deprecated}: the \code{wnba_stats_player_season_stats}
release tag (R-scraped, \code{Base}/\code{Advanced}/\code{Misc}/\code{Scoring}/\code{Usage}/
\code{Defense} measures) is superseded by the \code{wnba_stats_leaguedash} tag
(Python-scraped parameter cube, same 6 measure types plus \code{player_bio}
and a wide \code{player_master} mega). This function reshapes the cube back
into the old stacked-by-\code{measure_type} contract for compatibility; call
the cube's \verb{player_stats_*} / \code{player_master} assets directly with
\code{\link[=load_wnba_stats_leaguedash]{load_wnba_stats_leaguedash()}} for the full surface.

\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#deprecated}{\figure{lifecycle-deprecated.svg}{options: alt='[Deprecated]'}}}{\strong{[Deprecated]}} Loads season-level WNBA
5-man lineup statistics (\code{leaguedashlineups}-style outputs).
\strong{Deprecated}: the \code{wnba_stats_lineups} release tag (R-scraped,
\code{Base}/\code{Advanced} measures, 5-man only) is superseded by the
\code{wnba_stats_leaguedash} tag (Python-scraped parameter cube: 6 measure
types x 2/3/4/5-man). This function reshapes the cube back into the old
5-man \code{Base}+\code{Advanced} contract for compatibility; call the cube's
\verb{lineups_*} / \code{lineups_master} assets directly with
\code{\link[=load_wnba_stats_leaguedash]{load_wnba_stats_leaguedash()}} for the full surface.

\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#deprecated}{\figure{lifecycle-deprecated.svg}{options: alt='[Deprecated]'}}}{\strong{[Deprecated]}} Loads season-level team
statistics (\code{leaguedashteamstats}-style outputs). \strong{Deprecated}: the
\code{wnba_stats_team_season_stats} release tag (R-scraped, \code{Base}/
\code{Advanced}/\code{Misc}/\code{Scoring}/\code{Defense}/\code{Opponent} measures) is superseded
by the \code{wnba_stats_leaguedash} tag (Python-scraped parameter cube, same
6 measures plus \verb{Four Factors} and a wide \code{team_master} mega). This
function reshapes the cube back into the old stacked-by-\code{measure_type}
contract for compatibility; call the cube's \verb{team_stats_*} /
\code{team_master} assets directly with
\code{\link[=load_wnba_stats_leaguedash]{load_wnba_stats_leaguedash()}} for the full surface.

\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#deprecated}{\figure{lifecycle-deprecated.svg}{options: alt='[Deprecated]'}}}{\strong{[Deprecated]}} Loads season-level WNBA
standings (\code{leaguestandingsv3}-style outputs). One row per team-season.
\strong{Deprecated}: the \code{wnba_stats_standings} release tag (R-scraped) is
superseded by the \code{wnba_stats_leaguedash} tag's \code{standings} asset
(same underlying endpoint/params, Python-scraped) — this is close to a
pure passthrough.

Loads season-level WNBA draft picks scraped from the WNBA
Stats API (\code{drafthistory}-style outputs). One row per pick. Backed by
the \code{wehoop-wnba-stats-data} pipeline that reads raw JSONs from
\code{wehoop-wnba-stats-raw} and publishes parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{wnba_stats_draft} release tag.

Loads shot events scraped from the WNBA Stats API. One row
per shot attempt with legacy court coordinates, action/sub type,
distance, and made/missed result, carried through from the V3
play-by-play feed (not \code{shotchartdetail}). Backed by the
\code{wehoop-wnba-stats-data} pipeline that reads raw JSONs from
\code{wehoop-wnba-stats-raw} and publishes parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{wnba_stats_shots} release tag.

Loads the per-game \strong{inactive player} list scraped from the
WNBA Stats API -- the \code{InactivePlayers} result set of
\code{boxscoresummaryv2}. One row per inactive athlete-game pair, not a full
per-game roster: use \code{\link[=load_wnba_stats_player_game_logs]{load_wnba_stats_player_game_logs()}} for the
athletes who did play. Backed by the \code{wehoop-wnba-stats-data} pipeline
that reads raw JSONs from \code{wehoop-wnba-stats-raw} and publishes
parquet/rds artifacts to the \code{wnba_stats_game_rosters} release tag.

Coverage is thin by construction because the upstream result set is
thin: stats.wnba.com reports inactives for only a fraction of games,
and most heavily for 2006-2008 and 2021 onward. Season row counts range
from 1 (1997) to 610 across 184 games (2026); 2009-2012 carry fewer
than 10 rows each. A season with almost no rows is upstream sparsity,
not a download failure.

Loads game-level officials data scraped from the WNBA Stats
API (\code{boxscoresummaryv2}-style outputs). One row per official-game pair.
Backed by the \code{wehoop-wnba-stats-data} pipeline that reads raw JSONs
from \code{wehoop-wnba-stats-raw} and publishes parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{wnba_stats_officials} release tag.

Loads per-player per-game logs scraped from
\code{stats.wnba.com/leaguegamelog?PlayerOrTeam=P} (one row per
athlete-game pair: minutes, shooting splits, rebounds, steals, blocks,
turnovers, personal fouls, plus/minus). Backed by the
\code{wehoop-wnba-stats-data} pipeline that publishes parquet/rds artifacts
to the \code{wnba_stats_player_game_logs} release tag.

Loads season-level WNBA schedules scraped from
\code{stats.wnba.com/leaguegamefinder} (regular season + playoffs combined,
pre-rejoined home/away). Backed by the \code{wehoop-wnba-stats-data}
pipeline that publishes parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{wnba_stats_schedules} release tag.

Loads season-level WNBA play-by-play (V3), supplied by
\code{\link[=wnba_pbp]{wnba_pbp()}} in the upstream compile script. Backed by the
\code{wehoop-wnba-stats-data} pipeline that publishes parquet/rds artifacts to
the \code{wnba_stats_pbp} release tag.

